00:00:00,010 --> 00:01:33,930
[ Watch on kissFlix.co ]

1
00:01:56,040 --> 00:01:57,560
You scared me!

2
00:01:57,560 --> 00:02:01,639
Look, if you're sleepy,
just go upstairs to get some proper sleep.

3
00:02:01,639 --> 00:02:05,159
I wasn't sleeping. I was meditating.

4
00:02:05,159 --> 00:02:07,480
Meditating?

5
00:02:07,480 --> 00:02:08,839
Where's Ming Yu?

6
00:02:08,839 --> 00:02:10,360
Hasn't he been back for days?

7
00:02:10,360 --> 00:02:12,959
He hasn't been home
since he got back from Ma'ao.

8
00:02:12,959 --> 00:02:14,519
Don't act like you didn't know.

9
00:02:14,519 --> 00:02:16,280
Come on.

10
00:02:19,399 --> 00:02:23,239
Isn't this all part of your little scheme
with Zheng?

11
00:02:23,239 --> 00:02:26,480
Scheme? What scheme?

12
00:02:26,480 --> 00:02:29,839
Keep acting.

13
00:02:29,839 --> 00:02:31,640
You...

14
00:02:36,799 --> 00:02:39,000
You and him

15
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:42,400
had Ming Yu take his daughter to Ma'ao

16
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:45,240
just to push them together, didn't you?

17
00:02:45,240 --> 00:02:48,680
You think I can't see right through that?

18
00:02:48,680 --> 00:02:52,480
Zheng had the idea.
I couldn't exactly say no, could I?

19
00:02:52,480 --> 00:02:55,720
The point is,
we've watched You An grow up.

20
00:02:55,720 --> 00:02:57,080
We know her background well.

21
00:02:57,080 --> 00:03:02,063
That's exactly why
I don't want anything to do with them.

22
00:03:02,720 --> 00:03:07,480
Look, let the young people
figure it out themselves.

23
00:03:07,480 --> 00:03:12,720
Who knows. Maybe they'll hit it off in Ma'ao.

24
00:03:12,720 --> 00:03:14,559
I don't want to hear it.

25
00:03:14,559 --> 00:03:16,399
You two have some nerve.

26
00:03:16,399 --> 00:03:18,920
Ming Yu went there for work.

27
00:03:18,920 --> 00:03:20,399
It's a business trip.

28
00:03:20,399 --> 00:03:23,920
Yet you added a burden to his plate.
Honestly, you've gone too far.

29
00:03:23,920 --> 00:03:25,720
Well,

30
00:03:25,720 --> 00:03:28,799
you're against this only because
you don't like You An's mother.

31
00:03:28,799 --> 00:03:31,080
Stepmother.

32
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:37,760
So what if she's the in-law?

33
00:03:37,760 --> 00:03:42,440
We can keep our distance after that, can't we?

34
00:03:42,440 --> 00:03:44,560
In-law?

35
00:03:49,359 --> 00:03:51,920
<i>Surprise!</i>

36
00:03:51,920 --> 00:03:53,760
<i>So handsome!</i>

37
00:03:55,280 --> 00:03:56,920
<i>Ming Yu.</i>

38
00:03:58,320 --> 00:03:59,959
<i>Is she tired?</i>

39
00:03:59,959 --> 00:04:01,799
<i>Hurry up.</i>

40
00:04:01,799 --> 00:04:04,040
<i>Smile! Say cheese!</i>

41
00:04:06,880 --> 00:04:07,920
<i>You're 100 days old!</i>

42
00:04:07,920 --> 00:04:09,600
<i>How lovely!</i>

43
00:04:12,679 --> 00:04:15,239
Oh, my!

44
00:04:15,239 --> 00:04:19,560
What did I do in a past life
to deserve Dong Xian as my in-law?

45
00:04:19,560 --> 00:04:23,559
If heaven could send some destined girl
to capture Ming Yu's heart,

46
00:04:23,559 --> 00:04:26,440
I'd go vegetarian for a year!

47
00:04:30,880 --> 00:04:33,480
[Episode 12]
[A Complete Love Rat]

48
00:04:37,359 --> 00:04:38,920
She's not home, indeed.

49
00:04:38,920 --> 00:04:39,999
Good.

50
00:04:39,999 --> 00:04:42,480
How can we set up the surprise if she's here?

51
00:04:43,359 --> 00:04:45,400
- Let's go.
- Go.

52
00:04:47,520 --> 00:04:49,759
Is it ready? I'm hungry.

53
00:04:49,759 --> 00:04:52,280
Okay. Done.

54
00:04:52,280 --> 00:04:54,120
Time to eat.

55
00:05:02,080 --> 00:05:03,480
Nice cooking.

56
00:05:03,480 --> 00:05:05,760
You even carved the carrot?

57
00:05:08,879 --> 00:05:12,239
But you made so much.
I might not finish it all.

58
00:05:12,239 --> 00:05:14,425
You will finish it.

59
00:05:14,425 --> 00:05:17,440
Or I'll reduce your year-end bonus.

60
00:05:18,167 --> 00:05:19,270
What are you wiping?

61
00:05:19,270 --> 00:05:20,799
Lipstick.

62
00:05:20,799 --> 00:05:22,640
Don't want it ending up in the food.

63
00:05:22,640 --> 00:05:25,040
No need. It looks good.

64
00:05:26,400 --> 00:05:28,040
What's gotten into you today?

65
00:05:28,040 --> 00:05:30,040
Took a crash course in emotional quotient?

66
00:05:31,040 --> 00:05:32,693
Eat up.

67
00:05:32,693 --> 00:05:34,413
Thanks.

68
00:05:45,160 --> 00:05:47,400
And there's a cake, too?

69
00:05:48,102 --> 00:05:51,040
Mr. Fu, you're quite prepared.

70
00:06:01,656 --> 00:06:03,239
"Dear 'Captain' Ruan,"

71
00:06:03,239 --> 00:06:07,160
"if the road ahead is long,
may it be lined with flowers and light."

72
00:06:07,160 --> 00:06:12,359
"And if it's not, don't be afraid,
because we're right here with you."

73
00:06:12,359 --> 00:06:15,640
"Be a proud princess."

74
00:06:15,640 --> 00:06:20,480
"Love you forever."

75
00:06:24,330 --> 00:06:25,880
Actually,

76
00:06:25,880 --> 00:06:30,040
I ordered it on behalf of Hengshi Air.

77
00:06:30,040 --> 00:06:32,679
On this card are the best wishes
and appreciation

78
00:06:32,679 --> 00:06:36,440
from all the employees.

79
00:06:39,480 --> 00:06:40,840
Happy birthday.

80
00:06:40,840 --> 00:06:42,360
Thank you.

81
00:06:55,480 --> 00:06:56,879
Good job!

82
00:06:56,879 --> 00:06:59,600
- You're really something.
- Of course.

83
00:07:20,999 --> 00:07:24,040
Looks like "Captain" Ruan
doesn't want her bonus reduced.

84
00:07:24,040 --> 00:07:26,200
Who does?

85
00:07:30,200 --> 00:07:32,080
[Dong Xian]

86
00:07:38,759 --> 00:07:40,240
Hello?

87
00:07:43,920 --> 00:07:46,040
I'm good. I've already eaten.

88
00:07:46,040 --> 00:07:48,200
How do you know where I live?

89
00:07:49,947 --> 00:07:51,600
It's raining out there.

90
00:07:51,600 --> 00:07:53,520
You should head back.

91
00:07:54,960 --> 00:07:56,520
Okay.

92
00:07:56,520 --> 00:07:58,120
I'll be there soon.

93
00:08:04,920 --> 00:08:06,679
Boss, do you have an umbrella?

94
00:08:06,679 --> 00:08:08,520
Yes.

95
00:08:08,520 --> 00:08:12,080
- What do you need it for?
- I need to get something downstairs.

96
00:08:12,879 --> 00:08:14,080
It's pouring out there.

97
00:08:14,080 --> 00:08:15,720
I'll go.

98
00:08:17,080 --> 00:08:19,160
Thanks.

99
00:08:38,760 --> 00:08:41,880
Auntie Dong, sorry to keep you waiting.

100
00:08:41,880 --> 00:08:43,800
Ming Yu.

101
00:08:43,800 --> 00:08:46,000
Where's Ruan?

102
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:48,960
It's too rainy, so I didn't have her come down.

103
00:08:52,559 --> 00:08:56,040
Mr. Fu, may I ask you,

104
00:08:56,040 --> 00:08:58,920
what's your relationship with Ruan right now?

105
00:09:01,640 --> 00:09:05,479
At work, she's my employee.

106
00:09:05,479 --> 00:09:09,800
After hours, I'd say we're friends.

107
00:09:10,814 --> 00:09:12,814
Just friends?

108
00:09:12,814 --> 00:09:14,920
Auntie Dong,

109
00:09:14,920 --> 00:09:19,240
what we become depends on how Si Xian sees it.

110
00:09:19,240 --> 00:09:21,960
I can ask her when I go upstairs later.

111
00:09:24,160 --> 00:09:28,160
Alright. I'll leave it to you then.

112
00:09:29,520 --> 00:09:32,479
I'll make sure she gets your wishes.

113
00:09:32,479 --> 00:09:34,880
The rain's really heavy.
Be careful on your way back.

114
00:09:34,880 --> 00:09:36,920
Thanks, Ming Yu.

115
00:09:54,026 --> 00:09:55,666
You're back?

116
00:10:02,160 --> 00:10:06,599
Auntie Dong asked me a few days ago
if you were scheduled to work today.

117
00:10:06,599 --> 00:10:08,640
- Did you tell her?
- No.

118
00:10:08,640 --> 00:10:11,200
I have professional ethics, you know?

119
00:10:21,267 --> 00:10:23,800
It's the same as the one you ordered.

120
00:10:25,559 --> 00:10:30,240
"Don't mention... Dad."

121
00:10:37,959 --> 00:10:39,720
She's my mom.

122
00:10:43,392 --> 00:10:47,640
She just asked me what we are.

123
00:10:47,640 --> 00:10:49,603
And what did you say?

124
00:10:52,479 --> 00:10:57,600
I told her we're friends.

125
00:10:58,880 --> 00:11:00,559
Yes, that's right.

126
00:11:00,559 --> 00:11:02,480
We're friends.

127
00:11:08,520 --> 00:11:12,440
Since we're friends, come with me.

128
00:11:19,416 --> 00:11:21,400
I have a birthday gift for you.

129
00:11:21,400 --> 00:11:24,200
- You'll take it, won't you?
- What is it?

130
00:11:27,273 --> 00:11:28,953
Right this way.

131
00:11:34,760 --> 00:11:37,040
So many plane models!

132
00:11:44,272 --> 00:11:46,113
Do you like them?

133
00:11:47,520 --> 00:11:49,640
I thought you were giving me a real one.

134
00:11:49,640 --> 00:11:51,880
That's not out of the question.

135
00:11:51,880 --> 00:11:54,040
But there'd be conditions.

136
00:11:58,360 --> 00:12:00,839
Are these all your collection?

137
00:12:00,839 --> 00:12:02,640
Yes.

138
00:12:02,640 --> 00:12:04,599
You're really giving me one?

139
00:12:04,599 --> 00:12:07,280
- Take your pick.
- Then I won't hold back.

140
00:12:09,079 --> 00:12:12,360
I'll take...

141
00:12:13,360 --> 00:12:14,920
Z101.

142
00:12:14,920 --> 00:12:17,520
I never said you could only pick one.

143
00:12:17,520 --> 00:12:19,158
Really?

144
00:12:19,158 --> 00:12:22,800
You can take whatever you like in this room.

145
00:12:23,479 --> 00:12:25,079
What if I like everything?

146
00:12:25,079 --> 00:12:27,120
Does that include me?

147
00:12:29,663 --> 00:12:31,839
Fu Ming Yu!

148
00:12:31,839 --> 00:12:34,400
Are you trying to take advantage of me?

149
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:36,920
You were going to hit me again.

150
00:12:40,999 --> 00:12:43,000
And kick me too.

151
00:12:50,159 --> 00:12:51,879
Today,

152
00:12:52,799 --> 00:12:54,720
you look really beautiful.

153
00:13:18,679 --> 00:13:22,240
Well... I'll be going now.

154
00:13:43,760 --> 00:13:47,320
Surprise! Happy birthday!

155
00:13:48,640 --> 00:13:52,479
You scared me to death!

156
00:13:52,479 --> 00:13:54,440
<i>Your cake.</i>

157
00:13:56,920 --> 00:13:59,959
I don't want it. Keep it for yourself.

158
00:13:59,959 --> 00:14:01,240
<i>I'll leave it by the door.</i>

159
00:14:01,240 --> 00:14:03,120
<i>Remember to take it in.</i>

160
00:14:05,559 --> 00:14:07,160
Spill.

161
00:14:07,160 --> 00:14:09,439
We've been waiting for ages.

162
00:14:09,439 --> 00:14:10,520
Where were you?

163
00:14:10,520 --> 00:14:13,240
What were you doing with Fu Ming Yu?

164
00:14:13,240 --> 00:14:15,599
Tell us everything.

165
00:14:15,599 --> 00:14:17,200
I...

166
00:14:22,020 --> 00:14:23,060
Speak up.

167
00:14:23,060 --> 00:14:24,960
What did you eat for dinner?

168
00:14:25,599 --> 00:14:27,920
- Longevity noodles.
- Only noodles?

169
00:14:27,920 --> 00:14:30,479
A vice president like him ordered you noodles?

170
00:14:30,479 --> 00:14:32,360
It wasn't takeout.

171
00:14:32,360 --> 00:14:33,439
He cooked them for me.

172
00:14:33,439 --> 00:14:34,880
What?

173
00:14:34,880 --> 00:14:38,319
A vice president like him cooked for you?

174
00:14:38,319 --> 00:14:41,920
Alright, can we stop talking about food?

175
00:14:41,920 --> 00:14:44,120
Fine, you ask.

176
00:14:44,120 --> 00:14:45,620
Good.

177
00:14:46,760 --> 00:14:48,839
What exactly did you two do tonight?

178
00:14:48,839 --> 00:14:52,559
He cooked, I ate, I picked a gift,
and then I came back.

179
00:14:52,559 --> 00:14:53,593
- That's it?
- That's all.

180
00:14:53,593 --> 00:14:54,896
- Then why were you so flustered?
- Were I?

181
00:14:54,896 --> 00:14:56,000
You were.

182
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:58,040
When you came in and shut the door,
you were breathing hard.

183
00:14:58,040 --> 00:15:00,320
And your face was red.

184
00:15:01,120 --> 00:15:05,079
I swear, that's because I ran down the stairs.

185
00:15:05,079 --> 00:15:06,760
I didn't take the elevator.

186
00:15:06,760 --> 00:15:10,040
Could one floor make a woman
as strong as you pant?

187
00:15:10,040 --> 00:15:12,400
And he even got you a cake.

188
00:15:12,400 --> 00:15:16,880
One was from my mom, the other was from him
on behalf of the company.

189
00:15:16,880 --> 00:15:21,000
I've been at Hengshi Air for seven years,
and never gotten that kind of treatment.

190
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:22,920
Poor thing.

191
00:15:22,920 --> 00:15:24,600
Open it and see.

192
00:15:29,160 --> 00:15:30,360
It's smashed.

193
00:15:30,360 --> 00:15:33,320
It went through some stuff.
Still edible, though.

194
00:15:35,839 --> 00:15:38,040
Didn't you have any?

195
00:15:38,040 --> 00:15:40,640
Didn't get to. I came straight back.

196
00:15:40,640 --> 00:15:45,599
Why did you come back so early?
Was he trying something?

197
00:15:45,599 --> 00:15:47,173
No.

198
00:15:47,173 --> 00:15:52,679
I had to get the plane model back
before he changed his mind.

199
00:15:52,679 --> 00:15:53,680
Sure.

200
00:15:53,680 --> 00:15:56,439
"If the road ahead is long..."

201
00:15:56,439 --> 00:15:58,559
Aren't those my lines?

202
00:15:58,559 --> 00:16:00,560
They really are.

203
00:16:11,920 --> 00:16:14,120
She's got a good poker face.

204
00:16:14,120 --> 00:16:17,280
We've been grilling her all night
and got nothing.

205
00:16:17,280 --> 00:16:19,079
I don't think you need to ask anymore.

206
00:16:19,079 --> 00:16:21,719
Something's definitely going on.

207
00:16:21,719 --> 00:16:25,840
But one thing's for sure.
Your job is safe, right?

208
00:16:27,559 --> 00:16:29,040
Park yourself.

209
00:16:29,040 --> 00:16:30,640
I can't even tell whose car this is.

210
00:16:30,640 --> 00:16:32,720
I'm the one driving it every day.

211
00:16:34,839 --> 00:16:36,680
Drive safe.

212
00:16:48,760 --> 00:16:50,880
Today is Ruan's birthday.

213
00:16:50,880 --> 00:16:52,280
Xuan and I found out

214
00:16:52,280 --> 00:16:55,640
she's got something going on
with our vice president.

215
00:16:55,640 --> 00:16:57,199
Grilled her all night and she wouldn't crack.

216
00:16:57,199 --> 00:16:59,400
She's got a steel trap of a mouth.

217
00:17:02,319 --> 00:17:04,279
You've got a pretty tight mouth too.

218
00:17:04,279 --> 00:17:06,800
Still haven't confessed.

219
00:18:01,199 --> 00:18:04,720
<i>How much longer are you going to sleep here?</i>

220
00:18:41,999 --> 00:18:46,320
It must be the period, the hormones.

221
00:18:46,320 --> 00:18:48,520
That's the only reason I'd be thinking of him.

222
00:18:50,920 --> 00:18:53,279
Stop thinking about him.

223
00:18:53,279 --> 00:18:57,719
Period mode: lock up my heart.

224
00:18:57,719 --> 00:18:58,840
Stop thinking about him.

225
00:18:58,840 --> 00:19:00,560
Stop thinking about him.

226
00:19:10,880 --> 00:19:12,320
<i>No way.</i>

227
00:19:12,320 --> 00:19:14,640
<i>The hormones are really hitting hard.</i>

228
00:19:18,640 --> 00:19:20,680
Have you had breakfast?

229
00:19:21,393 --> 00:19:22,400
Yes.

230
00:19:22,400 --> 00:19:25,039
It's raining out there.
Might be hard to get a taxi.

231
00:19:25,039 --> 00:19:27,679
Get changed. I'll wait for you downstairs.

232
00:20:46,400 --> 00:20:47,679
Mr. Fu.

233
00:20:47,679 --> 00:20:50,360
Today's flight might not
be able to take off as scheduled.

234
00:20:50,360 --> 00:20:52,880
Should I notify them in advance?

235
00:20:52,880 --> 00:20:54,440
Got it.

236
00:20:58,759 --> 00:21:00,519
I'm going to the U.S. today.

237
00:21:00,519 --> 00:21:02,600
I'll be back in 10 days.

238
00:21:05,199 --> 00:21:07,360
So?

239
00:21:08,719 --> 00:21:10,760
Just letting you know.

240
00:21:11,679 --> 00:21:13,960
What's there to tell me?

241
00:21:26,959 --> 00:21:29,320
You can hop out here. I'll go park.

242
00:21:29,320 --> 00:21:33,400
But it's raining outside.
I'll have to walk in the rain.

243
00:21:33,400 --> 00:21:37,120
If I go to the parking lot,
you'll have to walk even further, right?

244
00:21:37,120 --> 00:21:38,679
Isn't this closer?

245
00:21:38,679 --> 00:21:40,959
Can't you drop me off at the entrance?

246
00:21:40,959 --> 00:21:43,640
- Which entrance?
- The main entrance.

247
00:21:44,800 --> 00:21:47,840
Usually only the president parks there, right?

248
00:21:47,840 --> 00:21:51,320
If I park there now
and another colleague sees us, what then?

249
00:21:51,320 --> 00:21:54,000
It's raining. I'm not getting out here.

250
00:21:54,696 --> 00:21:56,560
You're really harsh with your words.

251
00:21:56,560 --> 00:21:58,400
A taxi would pull up to that entrance too.

252
00:21:58,400 --> 00:22:00,160
Am I a taxi driver?

253
00:22:00,160 --> 00:22:02,400
If I pull up there, they'll recognize my car.

254
00:22:02,400 --> 00:22:04,600
You're afraid of being seen.

255
00:22:04,600 --> 00:22:06,679
I wasn't even thinking about that.

256
00:22:06,679 --> 00:22:08,600
That's exactly what you meant.

257
00:22:08,600 --> 00:22:10,479
If people see us and ask,

258
00:22:10,479 --> 00:22:15,600
I'll say I ran into you in the rain,
and you kindly gave me a ride.

259
00:22:15,600 --> 00:22:18,080
And honestly, who's going to ask me that?

260
00:22:18,080 --> 00:22:20,640
Are you new to the workplace?

261
00:22:20,640 --> 00:22:23,400
People gossip. They'll definitely ask.

262
00:22:23,400 --> 00:22:25,199
Then I'll have to waste time explaining--

263
00:22:25,199 --> 00:22:28,280
You don't want to explain,
so I have to walk in the rain?

264
00:22:29,640 --> 00:22:31,560
Take an umbrella.

265
00:22:36,920 --> 00:22:38,039
Yue Yang,

266
00:22:38,039 --> 00:22:43,759
if I were just any random colleague,
I wouldn't even get treated like this.

267
00:22:43,759 --> 00:22:46,160
Look, there's no "any random colleague."

268
00:22:46,160 --> 00:22:47,840
This seat has only ever been yours.

269
00:22:47,840 --> 00:22:50,920
No other woman has sat here,
not even any of the guys.

270
00:22:51,600 --> 00:22:53,800
- Really?
- Really.

271
00:22:53,800 --> 00:22:55,719
When you're not here,

272
00:22:55,719 --> 00:22:58,600
I keep a photo of you right there,
and a pile of snacks next to it.

273
00:22:58,600 --> 00:23:00,239
It's my way of telling people
this seat's taken.

274
00:23:00,239 --> 00:23:03,279
Her name is Jiang Zi Yue, right?

275
00:23:03,279 --> 00:23:05,160
Then swear on it.

276
00:23:07,966 --> 00:23:09,726
You swear.

277
00:23:11,279 --> 00:23:13,759
I know what you're thinking.

278
00:23:13,759 --> 00:23:18,080
You want people to know
how good we are together.

279
00:23:18,080 --> 00:23:21,439
But I think we can
keep that happiness between us, right?

280
00:23:21,439 --> 00:23:25,999
Why do we need the fanfare and
let other people watch and prove something?

281
00:23:25,999 --> 00:23:28,519
Besides, you're gorgeous and talented.

282
00:23:28,519 --> 00:23:30,640
Your colleagues are nowhere near your level.

283
00:23:30,640 --> 00:23:33,920
If they get jealous, I can't even imagine
what that'd look like.

284
00:23:33,920 --> 00:23:36,199
You and your sweet talk.

285
00:23:36,199 --> 00:23:38,520
That's all you've got.

286
00:23:42,959 --> 00:23:44,479
That's not all I've got.

287
00:23:44,479 --> 00:23:48,519
You only do things like this when I'm mad.

288
00:23:48,519 --> 00:23:50,480
Alright, don't be mad.

289
00:23:50,480 --> 00:23:52,280
You'll be late.

290
00:23:53,719 --> 00:23:55,320
Go on.

291
00:23:59,880 --> 00:24:00,881
I'm going.

292
00:24:00,881 --> 00:24:02,480
Go ahead.

293
00:25:25,519 --> 00:25:27,200
Thanks.

294
00:25:45,959 --> 00:25:47,600
What are you gawking at?

295
00:25:47,600 --> 00:25:49,160
Good morning, mentor.

296
00:25:49,160 --> 00:25:53,080
I just saw Ruan Si Xian
get out of Mr. Fu's car.

297
00:25:53,080 --> 00:25:54,560
- Really?
- For real.

298
00:25:54,560 --> 00:25:56,439
Mr. Fu's car is right there.

299
00:25:56,439 --> 00:25:59,000
He dropped her off himself.

300
00:26:05,320 --> 00:26:11,160
Mentor, I was literally giving her advice
the other day on how to go after him.

301
00:26:11,160 --> 00:26:12,560
What a joke.

302
00:26:12,560 --> 00:26:16,000
The clown was me all along.

303
00:26:18,200 --> 00:26:19,439
What time is your flight?

304
00:26:19,439 --> 00:26:21,560
Aren't you worried about being late?

305
00:26:21,560 --> 00:26:22,959
I'm running late!

306
00:26:22,959 --> 00:26:25,400
I've got to go. See you later.

307
00:26:49,520 --> 00:26:52,040
[Lu Ming]

308
00:27:17,679 --> 00:27:19,279
<i>Xiao Zhen.</i>

309
00:27:19,279 --> 00:27:21,920
<i>Please listen to me...</i>

310
00:27:34,439 --> 00:27:36,200
Lu Ming?

311
00:27:52,360 --> 00:27:58,240
[Jiang City]

312
00:27:59,360 --> 00:28:01,480
Yes, this one.

313
00:28:10,880 --> 00:28:11,959
Ni Tong, we're leaving.

314
00:28:11,959 --> 00:28:14,640
- Bye.
- Stay safe.

315
00:28:18,092 --> 00:28:21,519
When will this rain let up?

316
00:28:21,519 --> 00:28:24,720
With this many people waiting,
I'll be stuck here forever.

317
00:28:27,580 --> 00:28:29,160
Ni Tong.

318
00:28:29,160 --> 00:28:32,080
- Ruan.
- Get a taxi yet?

319
00:28:32,080 --> 00:28:33,240
Not yet.

320
00:28:33,240 --> 00:28:34,840
Still twenty-something cars ahead.

321
00:28:34,840 --> 00:28:35,946
Where are you going?

322
00:28:35,946 --> 00:28:37,280
A friend's picking me up.

323
00:28:37,280 --> 00:28:38,880
We can give you a ride.

324
00:28:39,560 --> 00:28:44,479
Ruan, does this friend happen to be Mr. Fu?

325
00:28:44,479 --> 00:28:46,910
Then you can wait for your own ride.

326
00:28:46,910 --> 00:28:49,439
What, I can't even ask?

327
00:28:49,439 --> 00:28:51,160
Xiao Zhen, where are you?

328
00:28:51,160 --> 00:28:54,000
I'm at the parking lot now.

329
00:28:59,759 --> 00:29:01,160
I've landed.

330
00:29:01,160 --> 00:29:03,480
How's the weather over there?

331
00:29:06,680 --> 00:29:09,280
[Recall]

332
00:29:10,560 --> 00:29:12,360
I must have been crazy.

333
00:29:12,360 --> 00:29:14,600
Why did I text him?

334
00:29:51,400 --> 00:29:54,719
The number you have dialed is powered off.
Sorry...

335
00:29:54,719 --> 00:29:57,280
Why's it off?

336
00:30:00,999 --> 00:30:02,320
<i>Hello, Ruan.</i>

337
00:30:02,320 --> 00:30:03,479
Hello, Xuan.

338
00:30:03,479 --> 00:30:06,759
I've landed, but I can't reach Xiao Zhen.

339
00:30:06,759 --> 00:30:08,679
<i>When did she leave the pub?</i>

340
00:30:08,679 --> 00:30:10,719
She left the pub quite a while ago.

341
00:30:10,719 --> 00:30:13,920
Said she was going to see Lu Ming,
and then head to the airport to pick you up.

342
00:30:13,920 --> 00:30:15,080
<i>Hasn't she shown up yet?</i>

343
00:30:15,080 --> 00:30:18,679
No. Her phone's off.

344
00:30:18,679 --> 00:30:20,320
What if something's happened?

345
00:30:20,320 --> 00:30:21,920
I've been waiting forever.

346
00:30:21,920 --> 00:30:23,360
Listen, don't panic.

347
00:30:23,360 --> 00:30:25,959
We've got Lu Ming's address in the group chat.

348
00:30:25,959 --> 00:30:28,679
<i>- I'll head over right now.</i>
- Okay, I'm coming too.

349
00:30:28,679 --> 00:30:30,600
Let's meet there.

350
00:30:38,200 --> 00:30:40,759
Ruan? What are you doing?

351
00:30:40,759 --> 00:30:42,719
Ruan, this is my ride.

352
00:30:42,719 --> 00:30:43,959
Where's your friend?

353
00:30:43,959 --> 00:30:45,199
My friend might be in trouble.

354
00:30:45,199 --> 00:30:46,640
I'll pay for everything.

355
00:30:46,640 --> 00:30:48,680
Go. Get in.

356
00:30:50,320 --> 00:30:53,439
- Hurry up.
- Wait...

357
00:30:53,439 --> 00:30:56,520
We're going to Ruifeng Garden.

358
00:30:58,959 --> 00:31:02,999
Come on, Ruan! I waited so long for this ride.

359
00:31:02,999 --> 00:31:04,640
Quiet.

360
00:31:05,713 --> 00:31:07,873
I can't reach Xiao Zhen.

361
00:31:08,476 --> 00:31:11,160
Please, step on it.

362
00:31:21,439 --> 00:31:23,280
Xiao Zhen!

363
00:31:23,880 --> 00:31:25,560
It's so late, why are you sitting here?

364
00:31:25,560 --> 00:31:27,840
- Where's Lu Ming?
- I've been waiting and waiting.

365
00:31:27,840 --> 00:31:30,279
I don't know where he went.

366
00:31:30,279 --> 00:31:32,719
He's not here.

367
00:31:32,719 --> 00:31:35,840
Don't cry. Crying won't help.

368
00:31:35,840 --> 00:31:38,200
- Xiao Zhen, where's Lu Ming?
- It's okay.

369
00:31:38,200 --> 00:31:40,120
Ruan.

370
00:31:40,719 --> 00:31:44,960
- There, there. It's okay. Don't cry.
- I can't find Lu Ming...

371
00:31:51,039 --> 00:31:53,720
Here. Drink this while it's hot.

372
00:31:59,640 --> 00:32:03,600
- I have one, too?
- You got caught in the rain too.

373
00:32:03,600 --> 00:32:05,400
Thanks.

374
00:32:06,160 --> 00:32:07,560
Ruan, don't waste it on her.

375
00:32:07,560 --> 00:32:10,439
She left you stranded at the airport for a guy.

376
00:32:10,439 --> 00:32:14,243
I never took her for that type,
ditching her friend for a man.

377
00:32:14,243 --> 00:32:15,920
I'm not that type!

378
00:32:15,920 --> 00:32:17,560
You're not that type?

379
00:32:17,560 --> 00:32:19,880
You're worse.

380
00:32:19,880 --> 00:32:22,280
- How could you leave Ruan--
- Xuan.

381
00:32:25,820 --> 00:32:27,400
Ruan.

382
00:32:27,400 --> 00:32:30,959
I'm sorry. I didn't mean to
leave you at the airport.

383
00:32:30,959 --> 00:32:32,759
I didn't know what to do.

384
00:32:32,759 --> 00:32:34,920
I wanted to ask him face to face.

385
00:32:34,920 --> 00:32:39,622
Why does he ignore me every time he goes out,
doesn't reply to texts, doesn't pick up calls?

386
00:32:39,622 --> 00:32:43,444
Why hasn't he contacted me in so long?

387
00:32:43,444 --> 00:32:46,959
And my phone died. I got carried away.

388
00:32:46,959 --> 00:32:48,439
I didn't mean to put you second.

389
00:32:48,439 --> 00:32:51,977
Okay, I know you're not that kind of person.

390
00:32:51,977 --> 00:32:54,809
Si Xiao Zhen, is it worth it for a jerk?

391
00:32:54,809 --> 00:32:56,759
"Going out," "business trips"...

392
00:32:56,759 --> 00:32:58,679
These are the warm-ups before he ghosts you.

393
00:32:58,679 --> 00:33:00,800
Once they're out, they're wild.

394
00:33:00,800 --> 00:33:03,880
And they can conveniently tell you
they're "too busy."

395
00:33:03,880 --> 00:33:05,640
He doesn't care one bit about how you feel.

396
00:33:05,640 --> 00:33:06,999
He's not like that.

397
00:33:06,999 --> 00:33:10,840
- He always told me--
- Sweet talk's called sweet for a reason.

398
00:33:11,679 --> 00:33:14,080
Tong Le, come over here.

399
00:33:17,920 --> 00:33:22,240
Give us a few lines of your best sweet talk.

400
00:33:33,360 --> 00:33:36,439
Before I met you,
I didn't really have a plan for my life.

401
00:33:36,439 --> 00:33:37,880
But now I do.

402
00:33:37,880 --> 00:33:40,959
I've selfishly included you in my future.

403
00:33:40,959 --> 00:33:45,999
I'm not the gentle type, but for you, I can be.

404
00:33:45,999 --> 00:33:51,199
I didn't even know how to make drinks,
but I learned it, just so I could stay here.

405
00:33:51,199 --> 00:33:55,120
So whether you think it's love at first sight
or just pure obsession,

406
00:33:55,120 --> 00:33:56,121
I don't care.

407
00:33:56,121 --> 00:33:59,239
I just want you to know, for you,
I'd change everything about myself--

408
00:33:59,239 --> 00:34:00,880
- Alright, that's enough.
- I...

409
00:34:02,439 --> 00:34:05,560
See? Men will say anything to charm a woman.

410
00:34:05,560 --> 00:34:08,200
- I meant every word.
- Are you done?

411
00:34:08,200 --> 00:34:10,039
Finished the glasses? Go work.

412
00:34:10,039 --> 00:34:11,680
Got it.

413
00:34:13,360 --> 00:34:17,439
Men will say anything to get what they want.

414
00:34:17,439 --> 00:34:19,680
One minute they're all over you,

415
00:34:19,680 --> 00:34:22,920
the next they give you the cold shoulder
without a second thought.

416
00:34:22,920 --> 00:34:25,479
You ask them
why they don't remember the good times.

417
00:34:25,479 --> 00:34:27,119
What good times?

418
00:34:27,119 --> 00:34:30,120
You made all that up in your head.

419
00:34:30,120 --> 00:34:32,119
Fine.

420
00:34:32,119 --> 00:34:36,720
For argument's sake,
are you even officially together?

421
00:34:36,720 --> 00:34:38,920
Has he ever confessed to you?

422
00:34:40,440 --> 00:34:43,360
Silence is how adults say goodbye.

423
00:34:43,360 --> 00:34:45,960
And you were dumb enough
to go knock on his door

424
00:34:45,960 --> 00:34:48,602
and make yourself look this pathetic.

425
00:34:51,439 --> 00:34:53,520
<i>Today,</i>

426
00:34:54,150 --> 00:34:56,120
<i>you look really beautiful.</i>

427
00:34:56,120 --> 00:34:57,800
<i>I'm going to the U.S. today.</i>

428
00:34:57,800 --> 00:35:00,439
<i>I'll be back in 10 days.</i>

429
00:35:00,439 --> 00:35:01,578
<i>Scumbag.</i>

430
00:35:01,578 --> 00:35:03,812
<i>A complete love rat.</i>

431
00:35:03,812 --> 00:35:07,119
Back then, didn't Ruan and I both tell you
this guy was unreliable?

432
00:35:07,119 --> 00:35:09,840
Didn't we both tell you to take it slow?

433
00:35:09,840 --> 00:35:12,124
You didn't listen to a word.

434
00:35:12,124 --> 00:35:16,419
The tears you're shedding now
are the water you let into your head back then.

435
00:35:16,419 --> 00:35:17,800
Let them out.

436
00:35:17,800 --> 00:35:22,999
Maybe I made him invest too much time

437
00:35:22,999 --> 00:35:26,320
without giving him anything back?
Maybe he just ran out of patience?

438
00:35:26,320 --> 00:35:28,840
Now you're still blaming yourself?

439
00:35:28,840 --> 00:35:32,039
Ghosting is a classic move.

440
00:35:32,039 --> 00:35:33,680
He's already moved on to the next one,

441
00:35:33,680 --> 00:35:36,640
and you're still trying to figure out
what you did wrong?

442
00:35:44,439 --> 00:35:46,400
Alright, Xiao Zhen.

443
00:35:46,400 --> 00:35:49,800
Whatever the reason, you have to face reality.

444
00:35:49,800 --> 00:35:54,999
Sudden disappearances like this
usually mean one of three things.

445
00:35:54,999 --> 00:35:57,709
First, he found someone else.

446
00:35:57,709 --> 00:36:01,400
Second, his real girlfriend found out.

447
00:36:01,400 --> 00:36:04,880
Third, most likely, he's in jail.

448
00:36:04,880 --> 00:36:06,720
Which one is it, then?

449
00:36:06,720 --> 00:36:08,800
Doesn't matter which one.

450
00:36:08,800 --> 00:36:12,760
You need to act
like this guy never even existed.

451
00:36:14,590 --> 00:36:16,064
Alright, stop being sad.

452
00:36:16,064 --> 00:36:19,280
Finish this drink, forget the jerk.

453
00:36:19,280 --> 00:36:22,600
Goodbye to him, on to the next.

454
00:36:32,123 --> 00:36:34,023
You're so good to me.

455
00:36:34,023 --> 00:36:35,280
Still cold?

456
00:36:35,280 --> 00:36:36,960
Not anymore.

457
00:36:39,560 --> 00:36:43,800
[United States]

458
00:36:43,800 --> 00:36:46,479
So, what's the deal with Charles?

459
00:36:46,479 --> 00:36:48,360
Leaving us hanging like this. Pretty rude.

460
00:36:48,360 --> 00:36:50,069
He's late.

461
00:36:50,069 --> 00:36:53,528
We're not here on behalf of the company,

462
00:36:54,119 --> 00:36:56,079
and he knows why I came.

463
00:36:56,079 --> 00:36:57,680
He's putting on airs.

464
00:36:57,680 --> 00:37:00,280
If I'd known,
we wouldn't have to come this early.

465
00:37:00,280 --> 00:37:01,941
You haven't eaten a thing.

466
00:37:01,941 --> 00:37:06,000
We could've grabbed something
instead of just sitting here waiting.

467
00:37:06,000 --> 00:37:07,479
Let's wait a bit.

468
00:37:07,479 --> 00:37:10,834
If we didn't come early,
we might not catch him at all.

469
00:37:10,834 --> 00:37:13,959
When he shows up, your jet lag kicks in.

470
00:37:13,959 --> 00:37:15,559
Can you hold up?

471
00:37:15,559 --> 00:37:18,519
I was thinking I could take you to Chinatown.

472
00:37:18,519 --> 00:37:20,280
There's an amazing hotpot place.

473
00:37:20,280 --> 00:37:24,120
Little stools, little tables, spicy hotpot...

474
00:37:24,120 --> 00:37:29,120
- Even local Chinese go there. Really good--
- I don't eat spicy food.

475
00:37:45,138 --> 00:37:47,560
How did they both get this drunk?

476
00:37:47,560 --> 00:37:50,559
Tong Le, what did you put in that ginger tea?

477
00:37:50,559 --> 00:37:51,800
Red wine.

478
00:37:51,800 --> 00:37:54,750
Red wine? Which bottle?

479
00:37:54,750 --> 00:37:58,280
The one under your cabinet.

480
00:37:58,280 --> 00:37:59,800
Saw you hadn't finished it till today.

481
00:37:59,800 --> 00:38:01,800
Didn't want it to go to waste.

482
00:38:01,800 --> 00:38:03,360
No.

483
00:38:03,360 --> 00:38:05,600
My Romanée-Conti.

484
00:38:18,960 --> 00:38:21,400
And now it tastes like ginger.

485
00:38:24,280 --> 00:38:27,640
What a waste.

486
00:38:31,639 --> 00:38:32,959
Go!

487
00:38:32,959 --> 00:38:34,800
Easy!

488
00:38:34,800 --> 00:38:35,959
- Where's the light?
- Light...

489
00:38:35,959 --> 00:38:38,079
There, on your left.

490
00:38:38,079 --> 00:38:39,880
Close the door!

491
00:38:39,880 --> 00:38:42,200
The suitcase! Almost forgot it.

492
00:38:42,200 --> 00:38:43,680
Wait, change your shoes!

493
00:38:43,680 --> 00:38:45,119
Seriously?

494
00:38:45,119 --> 00:38:48,200
I can barely hold her up.
I'll get her on the bed.

495
00:38:48,880 --> 00:38:51,119
Easy.

496
00:38:51,119 --> 00:38:52,400
My goodness.

497
00:38:52,400 --> 00:38:53,760
- Easy.
- Give me a hand.

498
00:38:53,760 --> 00:38:55,440
Careful.

499
00:38:56,880 --> 00:38:58,079
There we go. Wait outside.

500
00:38:58,079 --> 00:39:00,079
I'll change her clothes.

501
00:39:00,079 --> 00:39:02,640
Alright, I'll grab some water.

502
00:39:19,240 --> 00:39:22,760
Tong Le, from now on, whenever they come,

503
00:39:22,760 --> 00:39:25,920
you're not to give them a drop of alcohol

504
00:39:26,652 --> 00:39:28,733
unless they're accompanied.

505
00:39:30,813 --> 00:39:32,413
Did you...

506
00:39:59,360 --> 00:40:01,320
What did you say?

507
00:40:01,320 --> 00:40:06,880
I said, drinking's better with company.

508
00:40:14,519 --> 00:40:16,440
Who do you want to have with you?

509
00:40:17,439 --> 00:40:19,080
How about me?

510
00:40:54,880 --> 00:40:58,200
Is there no internet over there?

511
00:41:00,720 --> 00:41:03,000
Can't send me a message?

512
00:41:03,000 --> 00:41:06,240
[Fu Ming Yu]

513
00:41:06,240 --> 00:41:08,360
Thank you very much. Nice to meet you guys.

514
00:41:08,360 --> 00:41:09,840
- Likewise.
- Have a nice trip. See you.

515
00:41:09,840 --> 00:41:11,439
- See you.
- See you. Bye, guys.

516
00:41:11,439 --> 00:41:13,464
See you.

517
00:41:13,464 --> 00:41:16,640
This afternoon, right? Okay.

518
00:41:21,840 --> 00:41:22,841
Hello?

519
00:41:22,841 --> 00:41:24,520
<i>Hello?</i>

520
00:41:25,439 --> 00:41:28,240
<i>Is this Fu Ming Yu?</i>

521
00:41:28,240 --> 00:41:31,680
- It's me.
- So your phone didn't get lost.

522
00:41:31,680 --> 00:41:34,920
<i>And it's not broken either.</i>

523
00:41:34,920 --> 00:41:37,880
<i>Every time you go on a business trip,
you pretend to be busy,</i>

524
00:41:37,880 --> 00:41:40,639
and you don't send a single message.

525
00:41:40,639 --> 00:41:43,583
You're but a player.

526
00:41:43,583 --> 00:41:46,920
Get a little taste, and you're gone.

527
00:41:49,639 --> 00:41:52,800
- Have you been drinking?
- No.

528
00:41:52,800 --> 00:41:55,360
I'm perfectly clear-headed.

529
00:41:55,360 --> 00:41:59,699
I'm about to make a major decision.

530
00:41:59,699 --> 00:42:02,480
I'm kicking you out.

531
00:42:02,480 --> 00:42:05,200
<i>Kick you out of my head.</i>

532
00:42:05,200 --> 00:42:07,800
<i>I'm done thinking about you.</i>

533
00:42:07,800 --> 00:42:09,800
<i>You jerk.</i>

534
00:42:09,800 --> 00:42:14,200
<i>You think buying me a birthday cake
gives you some kind of status?</i>

535
00:42:14,200 --> 00:42:15,720
<i>Not even close.</i>

536
00:42:15,720 --> 00:42:18,439
I'm locking my heart up.

537
00:42:18,439 --> 00:42:21,600
I'm going to be immune.

538
00:42:22,279 --> 00:42:24,680
I'm listening to Xuan,

539
00:42:24,680 --> 00:42:27,720
no more believing men's sweet talk.

540
00:42:27,720 --> 00:42:29,119
<i>No more believing you.</i>

541
00:42:29,119 --> 00:42:31,000
<i>Scumbag.</i>

542
00:42:42,760 --> 00:42:43,959
Mr. Fu.

543
00:42:43,959 --> 00:42:46,280
We need to cut this trip short.

544
00:42:46,280 --> 00:42:47,999
I need to get back earlier.

545
00:42:47,999 --> 00:42:49,960
Are we skipping hotpot?

